# --- s031 Book I d.6 q.un. = Ord. I d.6 q.un. (Vat. IV)
n("n533","s031-01","Circa sextam distinctionem","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 6 q. un. (ed. Vat. IV), *utrum Deus Pater genuit Deum Filium voluntate*; cf. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 6 (*utrum Pater genuerit Filium voluntate vel necessitate*).","certain")
n("n534","s031-01","Hylarius. 15. de tri.","la","source","Hilary's *De Trinitate* has twelve books, so *XV* cannot be right. The dictum about the Father communicating all things to the Son *caritate et natura* is not yet located. It is perhaps from *De synodis* or *De Trin.* IX.","to-verify")
n("n535","s031-01","Aug. 3°. de tri.","la","source","The condemnation of Eunomius (*Filium Dei non natura sed voluntate*) is in Augustine, *De Trin.* XV 20.38, not book III. A's *3°* is presumably a misreading of *15°* (*xv*).","to-verify")
n("n536","s031-01","Eugomii","la","textual","So A, for *Eunomii* (Eunomius of Cyzicus).","certain")
n("n537","s031-02","fratre Johanne Roditon","la","historical","John of Rodington OFM (d. 1348), Oxford master and provincial minister, who wrote a commentary on the *Sentences*. Gorris traces the nominal/adverbial distinction of *voluntate* to Rodington, I d. 6 q. un. a. 3. This is a rare citation of Rodington in a fifteenth-century Scotist compendium. The reference is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n538","s031-02","Hic est Thomas prima parte summe. q. 34. articulo. 1.","la","source","Aquinas, *ST* I q. 34 a. 1 (whether *Verbum* is a personal name in God) distinguishes *intelligere* and *dicere*. The pairing with Henry, *Quodl.* VI q. 2, for the anonymous *quidam doctor* of *Ord.* I d. 6 is Gorris's own and is to be checked against the Vatican apparatus.","to-verify")
n("n539","s031-02","Henricus quodlibeto. 2°. q. 5.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* II q. 5. It is not checked whether this is the *quidam doctor* on the *intentio copulans parentem cum prole* (Augustine, *De Trin.* XI 7.12; cf. IX 12.18).","to-verify")
n("n540","s031-02","Hy","la","textual","So printed, for *Hi*.","certain")
n("n541","s031-03","in primo signo originis","la","source","The doctrine of *signa originis* (instants of nature within the divine life) and of the Father willing in the first instant what he begets in the second follows the solution of *Ord.* I d. 6.","to-verify")
n("n542","s031-04","in epistola ad Orosium","la","source","The *Dialogus quaestionum LXV Orosii et Augustini* (Pseudo-Augustine), q. 7, as cited by Lombard and Scotus. The exact wording *voluntas patris preire scientiam non potest* is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n543","s031-04","Generatio est opus nature","la","source","John Damascene, *De fide orthodoxa* I c. 8 (Burgundio's translation): generation is a work of nature, creation a work of will.","certain")
n("n544","s031-06","de exigentia","la","textual","A reads *de 4°. scilicet de exigentia*, but the fourth necessity listed is *indigentie*. The translation reads ‘indigence’, as the reason given (*si indigens*) requires.","certain")
n("n545","s031-07","respectu voluntatis pone alias quatuor","la","textual","The four conclusions just given concern the intellect. *voluntatis* (first occurrence) is presumably a slip for *intellectus*, and the translation so takes it.","uncertain")
n("n546","s031-07","verbum nunquam est nisi a dicente","la","source","The idea is Augustinian (*De Trin.* VII 1.2 and XV 14.23). The exact source of the wording is not found.","to-verify")
n("n547","s031-10","Godofredum quodlibeto. 5. q. 4.","la","source","Godfrey of Fontaines, *Quodl.* V q. 4. The reference is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n548","s031-11","memoria fecunda","la","source","The Scotist *memoria fecunda* (intellect plus essence as present object) is the principle of the production of the Word: *Ord.* I d. 2 p. 2 qq. 1–4 nn. 221ff.; *Ord.* I d. 6.","certain")
n("n549","s031-11","copulat parentem cum prole","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* XI 7.12 (the will *copulatrix* of parent and offspring), on the trinity of memory, understanding and will.","certain")
n("n550","s031-01","Hilary","en","translation","See note on the Latin reference. *caritas* is here the divine charity that is the essence; this is how the reply at §s031-11 takes it.")
n("n551","s031-06","[indigence]","en","translation","A *exigentia*; corrected from the list just given.")
n("n552","s031-07","with respect to the [intellect]","en","translation","A *voluntatis*, corrected; see the Latin note.")
n("n553","s031-03","instant of origin","en","translation","*signum originis*: a ‘sign’ or instant in the order of origin (not of time), in which one thing is prior by nature to another.")

# --- B collation (full): B44R–B46R
n("n948","s031-02","aliter dicit quidam doctor","la","textual","B: *dicit quidam doctor aliter*.","certain")
upd("n537", append=" B reads *Johēz roditoris* (genitive of a form *Roditor*), which supports the identification with Rodington.")
n("n949","s031-04","Quarto dicetur vtrum","la","textual","B: *Quarto vtrum* (om. *dicetur*).","certain")
n("n950","s031-05","qui non variat rationem formalem","la","textual","B: *qui non nominat rationem formalem* (*q nō noīat*). A's *variat* is clear in the print. B's reading gives an easier sense (the adverb does not name a formal ratio), but A's makes sense too, and A is kept.","certain")
upd("n544", append=" B also reads *exigentia*, so the slip is shared by both printings.")
upd("n546", append=" B reads *Verbum nunquam est sine adiciente* (*sine adiciēte*), apparently a corruption of A's reading.")
n("n952","s031-07","ergo intellectus elicit verbum","la","textual","B: *ergo intellectio elicit verbum*.","certain")
upd("n545", append=" B reads *respectu voluntatis potentie*, so it offers no support for *intellectus*.")
